&lt;p&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cts.businesswire.com/ct/CT?id=smartlink&amp;amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fionq.com%2F&amp;amp;esheet=54451094&amp;amp;newsitemid=20260316477473&amp;amp;lan=en-US&amp;amp;anchor=IonQ%2C+Inc&amp;amp;index=7&amp;amp;md5=0818ffbedc6dbad8c4d1611ac94c2a0f&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;IonQ, Inc&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;. [NYSE: IONQ] is the world’s leading quantum platform and merchant supplier - delivering integrated quantum solutions across computing, networking, sensing, and security. IonQ’s newest generation of quantum computers, the IonQ Tempo, is the latest in a line of cutting-edge systems that have been helping customers and partners including &lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cts.businesswire.com/ct/CT?id=smartlink&amp;amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fionq.com%2Fnews%2Fionq-speeds-quantum-accelerated-drug-development-application-with&amp;amp;esheet=54451094&amp;amp;newsitemid=20260316477473&amp;amp;lan=en-US&amp;amp;anchor=Amazon+Web+Services%2C&amp;amp;index=8&amp;amp;md5=a7f94ee9b71a392dca3cd6c413722e51&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Amazon Web Services, &lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cts.businesswire.com/ct/CT?id=smartlink&amp;amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fionq.com%2Fnews%2Fionq-speeds-quantum-accelerated-drug-development-application-with&amp;amp;esheet=54451094&amp;amp;newsitemid=20260316477473&amp;amp;lan=en-US&amp;amp;anchor=and&amp;amp;index=9&amp;amp;md5=2bed627b388878763f41ffe0e4edb16c&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;and &lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cts.businesswire.com/ct/CT?id=smartlink&amp;amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fionq.com%2Fnews%2Fionq-speeds-quantum-accelerated-drug-development-application-with&amp;amp;esheet=54451094&amp;amp;newsitemid=20260316477473&amp;amp;lan=en-US&amp;amp;anchor=AstraZeneca&amp;amp;index=10&amp;amp;md5=757c1f2c2ec94cf3982700106122164f&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;AstraZeneca&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt; achieve 20x performance results and accelerate innovation in drug discovery, materials science, financial modeling, logistics, cybersecurity, and defense. In 2025, the company achieved 99.99% two-qubit gate fidelity, &lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cts.businesswire.com/ct/CT?id=smartlink&amp;amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fionq.com%2Fnews%2Fionq-achieves-landmark-result-setting-new-world-record-in-quantum-computing&amp;amp;esheet=54451094&amp;amp;newsitemid=20260316477473&amp;amp;lan=en-US&amp;amp;anchor=setting+a+world+record+in+quantum+computing+performance&amp;amp;index=11&amp;amp;md5=32e9cb88afbd439026a352666cc72c91&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;setting a world record in quantum computing performance&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Headquartered in College Park, Maryland, IonQ has operations in California, Colorado, Massachusetts, Tennessee, Washington, Italy, South Korea, Sweden, Switzerland, Canada, and the United Kingdom. Our quantum computing services are available through all major cloud providers, while we also meet the needs of networking and sensing customers across land, sea, air, and space. IonQ is making quantum platforms more accessible and impactful than ever before. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;This role will be based at our office in Oxford, England, UK or can be remote within EMEA.&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Travel:&lt;/strong&gt; Up to 40% per quarter, depending on seasonal priorities.&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job ID: &lt;/strong&gt;1500&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Senior Director, Field Marketing EMEA will build and lead IonQ’s field marketing capability across EMEA, partnering closely with the wider Sales and Go-to-Market organisation to drive pipeline, accelerate strategic opportunities and strengthen customer engagement. This is a new M6 leadership role and a key appointment as IonQ continues to expand its commercial presence across the region.&amp;nbsp;This is a builder and operator role. The successful candidate will develop the EMEA marketing motion from the ground up, translating commercial priorities into high-impact campaigns, events, account-based marketing and executive engagement programmes. The focus is firmly on creating demand and measurable commercial impact, rather than owning broader corporate marketing functions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and execute the EMEA field marketing strategy, partnering closely with Sales and Go-to-Market teams to generate pipeline, accelerate strategic deals and increase engagement across priority accounts and markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead regional campaigns, account based marketing, strategic events and executive engagement programmes, ensuring activity is relevant to local markets and connected to commercial priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and lead a high performing field marketing organisation across EMEA, establishing the operating cadence, priorities and capabilities required as the region scales.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use data, pipeline performance and campaign ROI to inform planning, investment and prioritisation, creating clear accountability for marketing impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner across Sales, Product Marketing, Demand Generation, Events and the wider Marketing organisation while remaining focused on the EMEA commercial agenda.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Requirements:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;15+ years of marketing leadership experience in high-growth enterprise technology or emerging technology companies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record leading regional and/or international marketing teams across complex, multi-country markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep experience supporting enterprise and strategic sales motions, including long sales cycles and multi-stakeholder buying groups&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success partnering with enterprise sales organizations to drive pipeline, revenue growth, and strategic account engagement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional storyteller who can balance technical credibility with executive-level clarity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record in similar roles within the Americas region is strongly preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience operating in matrixed global organizations, influencing without authority&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable navigating cultural nuance, regulatory complexity, and varied market maturity levels&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep experience with account-based marketing, regional campaigns, executive engagement, and strategic events&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable balancing global strategy with hands-on regional execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data-driven decision maker with a bias toward measurable impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Compensation will vary based on individual factors such as education, qualifications, and experience of the final candidate(s), specific office location, and calibration against relevant market data and internal team equity. Posted base salary figures are subject to change as new market data becomes available. Our benefits include comprehensive medical, dental, and vision plans, matching 401(k), unlimited PTO and paid holidays, parental/adoption leave, legal insurance, and a home technology stipend. Details of participation in these benefit plans will be provided when a candidate receives an offer of employment.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At IonQ, we believe in fair treatment, access, opportunity, and advancement for all while striving to identify and eliminate barriers. We empower employees to thrive by fostering a culture of autonomy, productivity, and respect. We are dedicated to creating an environment where individuals can feel welcomed, respected, supported, and valued.&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;We are committed to equity and justice. We welcome different voices and viewpoints and do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, ancestry, physical and/or mental disability, medical condition, genetic information, marital status, sex, gender, gender identity, gender expression, transgender status, age, sexual orientation, military or veteran status, or any other basis protected by law. We are proud to be an Equal Employment Opportunity employer.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;US Technical Jobs.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;The position you are applying for will require access to technology that is subject to U.S. export control and government contract restrictions.&amp;nbsp; Employment with IonQ is contingent on either verifying “U.S. Person” (e.g., U.S. citizen, U.S. national, U.S. permanent resident, or lawfully admitted into the U.S. as a refugee or granted asylum) status for export controls and government contracts work, obtaining any necessary license, and/or confirming the availability of a license exception under U.S. export controls.&amp;nbsp; Please note that in the absence of confirming you are a U.S. Person for export control and government contracts work purposes, IonQ may choose not to apply for a license or decline to use a license exception (if available) for you to access export-controlled technology that may require authorization, and similarly, you may not qualify for government contracts work that requires U.S. Persons, and IonQ may decline to proceed with your application on those bases alone.&amp;nbsp; Accordingly, we will have some additional questions regarding your immigration status that will be used for export control and compliance purposes, and the answers will be reviewed by compliance personnel to ensure compliance with federal law.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;US Non-Technical Jobs.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Due to applicable export control laws and regulations, candidates must be a U.S. citizen or national, U.S. permanent resident (i.e., current Green Card holder), or lawfully admitted into the U.S. as a refugee or granted asylum. Accordingly, we will have some additional questions regarding your immigration status that will be used for export control and compliance purposes, and the answers will be reviewed by compliance personnel to ensure compliance with federal law.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you are interested in being a part of our team and mission, we encourage you to apply!&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SumUp is best known for helping small businesses get paid — our Consumer tribe builds the other half of that story. We make SumUp Consumer, the wallet app that lets everyday consumers pay SumUp merchants with a tap, send money to friends, track their spending and earn loyalty rewards along the way.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As we grow SumUp Consumer across new markets and features, we need sharp, reliable insight into how people discover, adopt and use the product — and how that behaviour translates into sustainable commercial growth. This includes understanding our acquisition funnel, improving activation and conversion, increasing customer value, and reducing churn.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a Product Data Analyst to join the Consumer tribe and become the analytical partner for SumUp Consumer. You’ll work closely with Product Managers, Designers and Engineers, alongside our Analytics Engineering team, to understand customer behaviour, shape product strategy, and connect product performance to business outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll help answer questions such as:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Which acquisition channels and customer segments generate the strongest long-term value?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Where do customers drop out of the journey from acquisition to activation?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;What drives repeat usage, retention and churn?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Which product changes improve conversion, customer value or commercial performance?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;How should we prioritise product investments across markets and customer segments?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you’re motivated by meaningful analytical work, enjoy translating complexity into clarity, and want to see your insights directly influence both product decisions and commercial outcomes, this role is for you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyse customer behaviour and product performance across the full consumer lifecycle — from &lt;strong&gt;acquisition and activation through engagement, retention, churn and reactivation&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities to improve conversion, customer value and sustainable growth using funnel analysis, cohort analysis, segmentation and behavioural analytics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with Product Managers, Designers, Engineers and Data teams to ensure decisions are grounded in robust analysis, customer insight and commercial understanding.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate the performance of customer segments, markets, channels and product journeys, helping the team understand where growth opportunities and commercial trade-offs exist.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support decisions that improve key business outcomes, such as activation, conversion, repeat usage, retention, churn, customer lifetime value and revenue-related metrics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct exploratory analysis to answer product and business questions, translating complex data into clear, commercially relevant recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define, monitor and communicate core SumUp Consumer KPIs, covering acquisition, activation, engagement, conversion, retention, churn and customer value.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, execute and analyse A/B tests and product experiments, assessing both customer impact and commercial impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain dashboards and reporting that stakeholders actively use, proactively surfacing trends, anomalies, performance risks and growth opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help Product Managers assess the expected impact of opportunities and evaluate whether product investments are delivering the intended customer and business outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Analytics Engineering to ensure KPI definitions, business logic and product instrumentation are accurate, scalable and trusted.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring a curious eye to AI and machine learning techniques, including LLM-assisted analysis, to speed up insight generation, customer understanding and product measurement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You’ll be great for this role if…&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have strong SQL skills and are comfortable querying, analysing and validating data in a cloud data warehouse such as Snowflake, BigQuery or similar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have hands-on experience with product analytics techniques such as funnel analysis, cohort analysis, segmentation and behavioural analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You understand the commercial drivers of a digital product, including customer acquisition, conversion, activation, retention, churn and customer lifetime value.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You can connect customer behaviour and product performance to business outcomes, and use data to identify growth opportunities and inform prioritisation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’ve worked on A/B tests or product experiments, with a solid grounding in the statistics behind them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re proficient in a visualisation tool such as Looker, Tableau or Power BI, with a track record of building dashboards that stakeholders actually use.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You can translate ambiguous product or business questions into structured analysis, and explain findings clearly to technical and non-technical audiences alike.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re comfortable assessing trade-offs, challenging assumptions and making recommendations based on evidence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re curious about how AI and emerging techniques can improve product measurement, experimentation, customer understanding and commercial decision-making.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re comfortable managing multiple workstreams and stakeholders, with strong prioritisation and a proactive communication style.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This role does not support Visa sponsorship and candidates must have the right to work in the UK.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Why you should join SumUp&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🌎 Opportunity to work with a truly global, multicultural team from our central London Bridge location, wrapped in historic charm and modern flair. This involves an office-first setup&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🌈 Commitment to Diversity and Inclusion: be part of a workplace that values and promotes diversity, fostering an inclusive environment where everyone&#39;s perspectives are respected and embraced&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🚀 Enrolment onto our Virtual Stock Option programme: you will own a stake in SumUp&#39;s future success&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🏖 Generous time off: enjoy 28 days of paid leave, plus bank holidays and special leaves&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;📚 A dedicated annual L&amp;amp;D budget for attending conferences and/or advancing your career through further education&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🏥 Health matters: private health insurance, including optical and dental&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🚗 Life made easier: salary-sacrifice commuter benefits via Gogeta&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;💼 Financial security: retirement scheme (SumUp matches 7% when you contribute 5%)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🛡 Peace of mind: life insurance from MetLife for 2× your salary&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🌴 Break4me: 1-month sabbatical after 3 years of service&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🔗 Referral Bonus: earn additional rewards by referring talented individuals to join the SumUp team&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About SumUp&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Be empowered to do more that matters.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At SumUp, we&#39;re on a mission to empower small businesses across the globe by providing simple and affordable tools that allow them to thrive. Today, over 4 million businesses in 37 markets rely on SumUp as their financial partner to manage payments, finance and customer relationships.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our commitment to small businesses is reflected in our diverse team of over 3,000 SumUppers from over 90 nationalities, united by global collaboration and an innovative mindset. Our core values lay the foundation for who we are and what we stand for, shaping our work culture and driving our success. We foster inclusivity and a continuous learning culture, providing a safe space for personal and professional growth. Our differences make us unique and strong as we strive to create an environment where everyone belongs and feels supported, no matter how they identify.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SumUp is proud to be an Equal Employment Opportunity employer, actively seeking and embracing diversity in our workforce. We don&#39;t make hiring or employment decisions based on race, colour, religion or religious belief, ethnic or national origin, nationality, sex, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, disability, age or any other basis protected by applicable laws or prohibited by company policy. Our commitment extends beyond recruitment to creating a safe and respectful workplace where harassment of any form is strictly prohibited. Discover more about our culture and opportunities on our careers website, and follow our journey on LinkedIn, Instagram, and TikTok.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Application Tip&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We recognise that candidates feel they need to meet 100% of the job criteria in order to apply for a job. Please note that this is only a guide. If you don’t tick every box, it’s ok too because it means you have room to learn and develop your career at SumUp.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;About Us&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:280}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SharkNinja&amp;nbsp;is a global product design and technology company, with a diversified portfolio of 5-star rated lifestyle solutions that positively&amp;nbsp;impact&amp;nbsp;people’s lives in homes around the world. &lt;strong&gt;Powered by two trusted, global brands, Shark and Ninja&lt;/strong&gt;, the company has a proven&amp;nbsp;track record&amp;nbsp;of bringing disruptive innovation to market and developing one consumer product after another has allowed&amp;nbsp;SharkNinja&amp;nbsp;to enter multiple product categories, driving significant growth and market share gains. Headquartered in Needham, Massachusetts with more than&amp;nbsp;4,100&amp;nbsp;associates, the company’s products are sold at key retailers, online and offline, and through distributors around the world.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI at SharkNinja &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At SharkNinja, we’re building an AI-native culture. We’re not waiting for the future; we’re creating it. Our people are expected to experiment boldly, adopt new tools, and continuously raise what’s possible to create meaningful impact for our consumers. If you believe the best way to do your job hasn’t been invented yet, you’ll fit right in.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Battersea, London | Hybrid – 3 days per week in office&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;From the company that brought you the &lt;strong&gt;Ninja CREAMi&lt;/strong&gt; and &lt;strong&gt;Shark FlexStyle&lt;/strong&gt;, SharkNinja is on a mission to redefine how consumers experience everyday household products. As a global product design and technology leader, we have built billion-dollar brands through relentless innovation and consumer obsession. Our portfolio spans Cleaning, Cooking, Food Preparation, Home Environment and Beauty, disrupting established categories and delivering five-star experiences to consumers worldwide.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for an exceptional &lt;strong&gt;Senior Consumer Insights Analyst&lt;/strong&gt; to join our high-performing UK team. You will ensure the consumer’s voice is central to product development and go-to-market decisions, translating research into clear recommendations that shape the next generation of SharkNinja products.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work closely with cross-functional and international partners in a fast-paced culture where insights have a direct and visible impact. If you are excited by innovation, comfortable challenging thinking and motivated by turning consumer understanding into better products, we would love to hear from you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Essential Functions&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a consumer insights lead within cross-functional teams, connecting consumer and market understanding to product development priorities and go-to-market strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the full research lifecycle, from developing discussion guides and surveys to moderating research, analysing results and delivering clear, actionable recommendations within budget and timeline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify unmet consumer needs and pain points, translating feedback into specific opportunities for innovation and product improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recommend the right methodology for each business challenge and manage external research partners to deliver high-quality, efficient execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Synthesise qualitative, quantitative and market inputs into compelling strategic narratives that influence product and marketing decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner across UK, European and global teams, ensuring local market perspectives inform broader product and commercial strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage multiple workstreams with a high degree of autonomy, adapting quickly as business priorities evolve.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Desired Skills and Experience&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Methodological Depth:&lt;/strong&gt; Strong understanding of qualitative and quantitative research, with the judgement to select the right approach for each business question.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Insight Synthesis:&lt;/strong&gt; Ability to move beyond reporting data and connect findings across multiple sources into a clear, compelling point of view.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic Orientation:&lt;/strong&gt; Proactively identifies what the business needs to understand and turns research into commercially relevant recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Early-Stage Innovation:&lt;/strong&gt; Comfortable working with ambiguity and using consumer insight to shape products during the early stages of development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Communication and Influence:&lt;/strong&gt; Presents recommendations confidently and concisely to cross-functional partners and senior stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Executional Rigour:&lt;/strong&gt; Effectively manages timelines, agencies, budgets and deliverables without compromising quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Adaptability:&lt;/strong&gt; Thrives in a fast-paced environment where priorities can shift and resourcefulness is essential.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;International Perspective:&lt;/strong&gt; Comfortable working across cultures and markets. Fluency in a second language, particularly a European language such as German, French, Italian or Spanish, is highly desirable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree, or equivalent qualification or professional experience, in Marketing, Psychology, Behavioural Science, Social Sciences, Business, Statistics or another relevant discipline. A postgraduate qualification is beneficial but not essential.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Approximately 4–7 years of consumer insights or market research experience, ideally within FMCG, consumer technology, durable goods or an innovation-led organisation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience applying core research methodologies such as concept testing, pricing research, packaging evaluation, segmentation and portfolio optimisation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience moderating focus groups, conducting one-to-one interviews and interpreting quantitative research.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with in-home usage tests, product experience research or in-store research environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience briefing and managing research agencies and other external partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal English communication skills. Proficiency in an additional language is highly desirable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work from our &lt;strong&gt;Battersea office three days per week&lt;/strong&gt; to support close collaboration and cross-functional impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Our Culture&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;At SharkNinja, we don’t just raise the bar—we push past it every single day. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Our Outrageously Extraordinary mindset&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; drives us to tackle the impossible, push boundaries, and deliver results that others only dream of. If you thrive on breaking out of your swim lane, you’ll be right at home.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;What We Offer&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
